{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage","id":23735,"title":"Divine Lineage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-05T07:03:53-08:00","id":23735,"title":"Divine Lineage","content":"So, the Scion rules say that the children of a deity are Scions of that deity. The children of Scions of a deity are also Scions of that deity. (p. 60 &amp; 79 of scion god book)<br /> <br /> &quot;Until he becomes a God, his own divine parent\u2019s predispositions are passed on to any children, and they may become Scions of their divine grandparent, if they receive an appropriate Visitation&quot;<br /> <br /> Two questions: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The wording is only for a single generation - Scions of the grandparent. Does the power of Ichor extend throughout multiple generations? if parent and grandparen were Scions, but never ascended, can the child become a Scion of the divine great grandparent?</li> <li>What happens when 2 scions with different divine parents have a kid?</li> </ol><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T07:29:13-08:00","id":23745,"title":"","content":"1) Usually in mythology, heroes are chosen from either children or grandchildren of gods. I'd think it would be pretty rare for power to translate any further unless the direct child of the god is uplifted.<br /> Think in terms of God &gt; demigod &gt; Hero. That's three generations. The game starts as God-to-Hero transfer.<br /> 2) Roll Legend for whose divine parentage is stronger in the grandchild? Have the grandparents compete in the Overworld for 'dips'? Or have both grandparents go 'dah that's so adorable' and be co-pilots? Your call. But try to find commonalities with that last one. Maybe limit it to five Power Thingies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T07:39:56-08:00","id":23751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage#post23735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording is only for a single generation - Scions of the grandparent. Does the power of Ichor extend throughout multiple generations? if parent and grandparen were Scions, but never ascended, can the child become a Scion of the divine great grandparent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially, no. Unofficially, you can feel free to have your story involve the great grandchildren, great great grandchildren, or even greater than all of that be visited and begin the journey of a Scion.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage#post23735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]What happens when 2 scions with different divine parents have a kid?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no rule that says what happens. I recommend you leave it open and allow ANY parent or grandparent of an unvisited potential Scion do the claiming. The child of Hermod could be visited by Hermod, Odin, or even Frigg. All three options could make for an amazing story. Heck, you could even throw Borr onto that list if the story really demanded it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T08:06:52-08:00","id":23764,"title":"","content":"Somehow I wonder now, whether Autolicus was an &quot;activated&quot; Scion. As his grandson, who received divine blood from greatgrandparent, most probably was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I must - so I can.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Learning makes life more rewarding and enjoyable;...the worst thing of all is ignorance</span>.</i> <div align=\"right\">Alfred the Great</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1425-vi-zet","name":"Vi-Zet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T09:12:44-08:00","id":23792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=23764#post23764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow I wonder now, whether Autolicus was an &quot;activated&quot; Scion. As his grandson, who received divine blood from greatgrandparent, most probably was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's worth diving too far down the rabbit hole. Both Autolycus...es were at least demigods. Jason and Odysseus' grandfather and the Autolycus who was an Argonaut (not the same person, if I recall correctly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T13:45:51-08:00","id":23949,"title":"","content":"Yes, they were different people, if I am not mistaken... though many versions place Odysseus' father among the Argonauts, so there is still some connection.)<br /> Though, if I am not mistaken, Autolycus the Hermes' son and Autolycus the Argonaut were different people.. but Autolycus the Hermes' son was grandfather of <b>both</b> Jason and Odysseus - through Polymede and Anticlea respectively.<br /> Mythological Greece makes whole world one big problematic family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I must - so I can.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Learning makes life more rewarding and enjoyable;...the worst thing of all is ignorance</span>.</i> <div align=\"right\">Alfred the Great</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1425-vi-zet","name":"Vi-Zet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T16:19:28-08:00","id":24059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=23949#post23949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they were different people, if I am not mistaken... though many versions place Odysseus' father among the Argonauts, so there is still some connection.)<br /> Though, if I am not mistaken, Autolycus the Hermes' son and Autolycus the Argonaut were different people.. but Autolycus the Hermes' son was grandfather of <b>both</b> Jason and Odysseus - through Polymede and Anticlea respectively.<br /> Mythological Greece makes whole world one big problematic family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, and the other Autolycus founded Sinope and was worshiped as its patron deity, IIRC.<br /> <br /> Been a long time since Western Civ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T16:35:29-08:00","id":24072,"title":"","content":"Is this a divine genetics problem? I'm so down to try to work this out. When the question of Scion+Scion babise happens, It would of course depend on whether given divine predispositions follow a given heritability model. (note that I'm specifically not referring to DNA, but it seems like Ichor will follow at least a somewhat comparable model). I don't have quite enough information to really begin, but if anyone would like to help out I'll happily try to model these out using Mendelian or Non-Mendelian Inheritance models.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T17:39:45-08:00","id":24082,"title":"","content":"I would say that a deciding factor of who the &quot;patron&quot; divinity is would also be done by Legend. Since this is a measure of how powerful the ichor in your body is, then this would play a deciding role in it. Whose power is greater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T18:16:25-08:00","id":24091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=24082#post24082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that a deciding factor of who the &quot;patron&quot; divinity is would also be done by Legend. Since this is a measure of how powerful the ichor in your body is, then this would play a deciding role in it. Whose power is greater?</div> </div> </div> </div>reasonable in circumstances where you have two Scions of equal legend, but what if you have two Scions of the same Legend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T20:50:19-08:00","id":24155,"title":"","content":"At that point, then I would go back to the simplest of gaming tropes...<br /> <br /> ROLL OFF!<br /> <br /> One die = mom's divine parent<br /> Second die = dad's divine parent<br /> <br /> Highest number wins.<br /> Tie = keeps rolling.<br /> <br /> The way all decisions should be made in an rpg...lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T04:58:48-08:00","id":24293,"title":"","content":"I'd rather not roll. I think that would just cut off one cool possibility. Why not leave them both open?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T07:23:11-08:00","id":24348,"title":"","content":"Can there be a possibility that such a child can receive a Visitation from any one of divine ancestors without any of them using <i>Scion Adoption Rite</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I must - so I can.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Learning makes life more rewarding and enjoyable;...the worst thing of all is ignorance</span>.</i> <div align=\"right\">Alfred the Great</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1425-vi-zet","name":"Vi-Zet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T07:46:50-08:00","id":24355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=24348#post24348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can there be a possibility that such a child can receive a Visitation from any one of divine ancestors without any of them using <i>Scion Adoption Rite</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>This option is best for everyone. Gods, Scions, players, gamemasters, and this forum. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T08:04:46-08:00","id":24363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=24348#post24348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can there be a possibility that such a child can receive a Visitation from any one of divine ancestors without any of them using <i>Scion Adoption Rite</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> The roll option is mostly used for npcs, anyways.<br /> <b>Tezcatlipoca and Quetzalcoatl competing for the immortal soul of their mutual grandchild IS ADORABLE.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T08:46:35-08:00","id":24372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=24363#post24363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tezcatlipoca and Quetzalcoatl competing for the immortal soul of their mutual grandchild IS ADORABLE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had a PC in my last game who basically ended up in this situation. Quetzalcoatl won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:42:59-08:00","id":24443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=24348#post24348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can there be a possibility that such a child can receive a Visitation from any one of divine ancestors without any of them using <i>Scion Adoption Rite</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW I want to say that only the actual Divine Parent(s) or Grandparent(s) can adopt without use of the Scion Adoption Rite. I also run this because the story potential of why a Scion was worth the trouble of hunting down a Magic God who was willing to perform the Rite AND why the &quot;Biological&quot; ancestor in question was willing to forsake the Scion is an amazing plot hook for PCs. <br /> <br /> For a Scion that has a potential of two or more divine peeps to be fighting, don't make it come down to a roll for your PCs. That's a cop out and incredibly unfair to the PC in question (unless they dgaf).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:14:31-08:00","id":24463,"title":"","content":"On a semi-related note, what are folks here's opinions on the idea of joint Visitations? There are definitely a few divine couples who seem to have relatively stable relationships and might, for some reason, Visit a Scion together. Can/should this happen? And if so, how could it work out mechanically? It's something I've been mulling over for a while with no really good answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:35:38-08:00","id":24496,"title":"","content":"I can totally see Vishnu and Lakshmi coming to a Scion to Visit him from a story point of view, but I do not think that it needs any mechanical changes. Or, to be more precise, I'd prefer if the two treated the Scion as their own, but he only got the mechanical benefits of one parent. Mostly because I have a feeling letting players custom design their Associations might get a bit crazy fast.<br /> <br /> Also, consider the fact that the few couples in mythology that are that loyal to each other will probably not be having biological Scions anyway, but would rather be adopting from more prolific parents like Indra. In such a case it seems more likely that instead of fighting over a single Scion they would probably just adopt one each and save everyone the trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:14:48-08:00","id":24595,"title":"","content":"I agree. While a Divine couple may <i>treat</i> their Scion as belonging equally to them both, that really can't happen. A mortal body can't hold two different types of Ichor without burning to a crisp. So one parent is the &quot;true&quot; parent. However it makes a <i>great</i> story for explaining non-Associated Purview Relics and other Birthrights that don't quite fit a single parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T21:24:03-08:00","id":24884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=24463#post24463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a semi-related note, what are folks here's opinions on the idea of joint Visitations? There are definitely a few divine couples who seem to have relatively stable relationships and might, for some reason, Visit a Scion together. Can/should this happen? And if so, how could it work out mechanically? It's something I've been mulling over for a while with no really good answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Achilles and I have had convos along this line of thought. In one game he ran we decided to allow the scion to pick 6 favoreds selected from either divine parent. Now allowing for such a thing in a full group..well like everything it would depend on the players involved. That said our main group, as you know, has a new system which I like far better as it doesn't lead to picking a parent for their favoreds, but because it's the story you want to play out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">At the end of the day, what works in <b>YOUR</b> story with <b>YOUR</b> players is what matters most. Not what someone on some forum says.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/328-phoenixfire","name":"PhoenixFire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar328_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T02:08:49-08:00","id":25006,"title":"","content":"Well, in my Scion game, we have one PC and one NPC who are developing this tragic love story. They are both Amtsukami (The PC being Hachiman and the NPC being Raiden) and so, of course, should they have a child then it would be Amtsukami. However, the further crinkle in this whole thing is:<br /> <br /> What if the two Scions are of different Pantheons? Would that factor into whether the divine ancestors could even cooperate, let alone compromise on things? Most Pantheons tend to stay away so that they do not Fatebound to one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T07:40:23-08:00","id":25096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/23735-divine-lineage?p=24463#post24463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a semi-related note, what are folks here's opinions on the idea of joint Visitations? There are definitely a few divine couples who seem to have relatively stable relationships and might, for some reason, Visit a Scion together. Can/should this happen? And if so, how could it work out mechanically? It's something I've been mulling over for a while with no really good answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really, really depends. Is the Scion in question a biological child of the union of the two parents? If yes, then the answer revolves around how you treat those types of kids. Are they A)Automatically Legend 9 Gods in their own right, like Hermes or Artemis? Or B) Are they Legend 2 Gods? Able to grow and develop along proper Scions which are half-mortal.<br /> <br /> If A or B then there's no problem with the child being able to pick favored from one or the other parent. Shoot, maybe even developing their own associated powers. Though, personally, I do run that a child of two gods is still only claimed by only one of them.<br /> <br /> But if the Scion is half-mortal, or well, half-god, then I'm with Telgar. You can't have a joint visitation because that other god, though united with their spouse, has no actual claim on your ichor and though they may adopt you into their family, they cannot Adopt you without the parent giving up claim. But, like Telgar said, it gives reason as to why you might have non-associated purviews and, as always, plot hooks.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}